\section{Results}
\label{sec:results}

We evaluate token pruning across five VLA models spanning three connector families on LIBERO-Object~\cite{liu2023libero} (10 tasks, 50 episodes each, 500 total). All success rates include Wilson 95\% confidence intervals for single-seed results and mean $\pm$ standard deviation for multi-seed results.

\subsection{Taxonomy Overview}
\label{sec:taxonomy_overview}

Table~\ref{tab:taxonomy} summarizes the five models and their pruning responses. The effective vision-to-LLM pipeline complexity, rather than the nominal connector label, determines pruning tolerance. A pure linear projection ($\pi_0$) is immune; a linear projection followed by a deep encoder (X-VLA) is threshold-graded (robust above a retention threshold, then graded decline); a multi-layer MLP degrades smoothly; and pixel-shuffle collapses catastrophically. Token importance heterogeneity (CV) tracks this ordering continuously: 0.038, 0.151, 0.215, 0.314. The pattern holds across a 16$\times$ range in model size (450M to 7B parameters), which suggests scale alone does not explain it.

A controlled comparison isolates the vision-to-LLM pipeline as the causal factor. $\pi_0$ and OpenVLA share the same token count (256), the same vision encoder lineage (SigLIP~\cite{zhai2023siglip}), and differ only in the connector: linear projection versus 3-layer MLP. At $k{=}0.1$ (retaining 10\% of tokens), $\pi_0$'s action loss \emph{improves} by 2.4\% while OpenVLA's degrades by 61\%. This 63-percentage-point gap is attributable to pipeline architecture alone. X-VLA's threshold-graded pattern (robust at $k \geq 0.9$, then degradation at $k{=}0.7$) further demonstrates that the \emph{effective} pipeline complexity---not just the connector label---determines pruning tolerance (Section~\ref{sec:linear_results}). OFT~\cite{kim2025openoft}, which replaces OpenVLA's action head but retains its 3-layer MLP connector, produces nearly identical attention entropy (0.667 vs.\ 0.661 for standard OpenVLA). The connector, not the action head, determines the attention structure that governs token dispensability.

